o current active or closed specification holds naming why. spec_at returns path, text and why, and lane_hold compares a lane's claim at its base with its current or closed copy at the requested revision, and staged_closes identifies index moves from active into any terminal home: docs/archive/work/complete, partial or cancelled, or the legacy docs/work equivalent.\"","+detail = \"bound_items reads each current Done-when item that only ticks or evidences a claim-time item as that claim-time item; digest binds the work-item id and those items as sha256:<16 hex>. covering reads verdict lines under review records only through the one accepted-verdict reader: only a bound verdict whose route recorded accepted and which parses valid contributes its Done-when line with outcome CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR and the digest; a failed, pending, unbound or other-class verdict covers nothing. An owner-confirmed or owner-overruled decision entry carrying that digest also covers; an unseen entry or retired reviewed key does not. claim_copy returns absent when its readable revision has no claimed specification for the work item, which releases every hold and produces neither a mint nor a brief; it returns unreadable when the revision or listed copy cannot be read, and unreadable_reason makes that a named hold at dispatch, hand close and merge and a mint or brief refusal. _copy_at gives both claim and current reads found, absent, or unreadable forms. blessing_owed owes when a readable current specification differs from a readable claim and has no cover; deleting its Done-when section reports every claimed item changed. An absent claim releases only for a row never claimed through that lane; an unreadable claim, unreadable current copy, or claimed row with no current active or closed specification holds naming why. spec_at returns path, text and why, and lane_hold compares a lane's claim at its base with its current or closed copy at the requested revision, and staged_closes identifies index moves from active into any terminal home: docs/archive/work/complete, partial or cancelled, or the legacy docs/work equivalent.\""," rationale = \"The same changed checklist is consulted at dispatch, hand close, merge and adjudication. One digest and covering predicate keep readers from accepting different texts or treating a verdict about an earlier text as a release.\""," test_refs = \"TC-325, TC-326\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3280,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3280,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-232\"]"," title = \"Combined sitting composes and validates kind-scoped adjudications\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/sitting.py;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_adjudicate.py\"","-code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope/GRAMMAR/DONE_WHEN_OUTCOMES/line_refusal/named_kinds/sitting_refusal/parse/requested_path/render_requested/read_requested/REQUESTED_SUFFIX;bind_requested\"","-detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. One parser reads a verdict into its kind lines: a combined sitting names exactly the kinds bound at reservation in <verdict>.requested, has exactly one kind-form lower-case section per bound kind and none other, and has exactly one complete own-kind machine line in each section; a single-kind verdict has no kind-form section and exactly one complete machine line. The coordinator verdict check and Done-when holds consume that parse, so an unbound combined verdict covers nothing. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope/GRAMMAR/DONE_WHEN_OUTCOMES/line_refusal/named_kinds/sitting_refusal/parse/requested_path/render_requested/read_requested/REQUESTED_SUFFIX/OUTCOMES/write_binding/accepted/accepted_part/accepted_at;bind_requested/_requested;record_outcome\"","+detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. One parser reads a verdict into its kind lines: a combined sitting names exactly the kinds bound at reservation in <verdict>.requested, has exactly one kind-form lower-case section per bound kind and none other, and has exactly one complete own-kind machine line in each section; a single-kind verdict has no kind-form section and exactly one complete machine line. The binding records pending at reservation and accepted or failed after a route runs the call; write_binding is its one writer and record_outcome its one route recorder and commit path. The coordinator verdict check, Done-when holds and held-rung re-attestation consume the one accepted-verdict reader, so only an accepted, bound, valid verdict counts; failed, pending, unbound or other-class verdicts cover nothing. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\""," rationale = \"A shared checkpoint reduces adjudication launches only if no constituent judgement loses its scope or grammar. One parser prevents composition, validation and later acts from interpreting the same sitting differently.\""," test_refs = \"TC-327\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":2827,"oldLines":11,"newStart":2827,"newLines":11,"lines":[" [test.TC-278]"," verifies = [\"SR-178\", \"SR-228\", \"LLR-278\", \"IF-091\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Driven on real git repositories made from scaffolds. An adjudication lane claiming an amendment row scoped to one requirement, whose act re-attests two amended requirements, is refused at merge naming the one outside the scope; an act re-attesting only the scoped row merges, and the same act claimed by a first-approval row is refused naming the row, since that lane holds no re-attestation scope. The held authority is read at trunk's tip rather than the merge base. A combined act across the same or different registries merges when each section acts only within its own kind scope and every copied registry has a flip or re-attestation; a copied registry neither section moved is WIDENED. With the rung held, a re-attestation without a verdict, of a row below approval, with a MEANING verdict, with a verdict that does not rule the row, with a named verdict file absent at the act's head, or with a verdict tagging the row both MEANING and CLARITY is refused by row, while a verdict ruling an approved row CLARITY merges. One act that approves a Drafted requirement and re-attests an amended one, claimed by a first-approval row scoped to the first and an amendment row scoped to the second, merges; the same act whose amendment row is scoped to another requirement is refused naming the re-attested row.\"","+method = \"Driven on real git repositories made from scaffolds. An adjudication lane claiming an amendment row scoped to one requirement, whose act re-attests two amended requirements, is refused at merge naming the one outside the scope; an act re-attesting only the scoped row merges, and the same act claimed by a first-approval row is refused naming the row, since that lane holds no re-attestation scope. The held authority is read at trunk's tip rather than the merge base. A combined act across the same or different registries merges when each section acts only within its own kind scope and every copied registry has a flip or re-attestation; a copied registry neither section moved is WIDENED. With the rung held, a re-attestation without a verdict, of a row below approval, with a MEANING verdict, with a verdict that does not rule the row, with a named verdict file absent at the act's head, with an accepted verdict that is invalid as a whole, or with a verdict tagging the row both MEANING and CLARITY is refused by row, while an accepted verdict ruling an approved row CLARITY merges. One act that approves a Drafted requirement and re-attests an amended one, claimed by a first-approval row scoped to the first and an amendment row scoped to the second, merges; the same act whose amendment row is scoped to another requirement is refused naming the re-attested row.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"Satisfies LLR-278 (parents SR-178 and SR-228): a re-attestation outside the amendment row's Adjudicates scope is refused at merge by name; on a held rung only a verdict ruling the row CLARITY permits it; and an act whose approvals and re-attestations each lie in the scope of the row claiming them merges.\"","+expected = \"Satisfies LLR-278 (parents SR-178 and SR-228): a re-attestation outside the amendment row's Adjudicates scope is refused at merge by name; on a held rung only an accepted verdict ruling the row CLARITY permits it; and an act whose approvals and re-attestations each lie in the scope of the row claiming them merges.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_reattestation_outside_the_amendment_scope_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_reattestation_inside_the_amendment_scope_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_without_a_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_its_verdict_rules_CLARITY_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py: