{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnQAAVUoBeVbTGmQ3f1X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All seven amended rows change meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=7`). I'd bless each new text, so I re-attested all seven.\n\nThe change: whether a verdict counts is now a recorded fact. Each verdict's `.requested` binding carries an outcome: pending when the path is reserved, then accepted or failed once the call runs. Every consumer reads that outcome through one reader instead of inferring it from the verdict text.\n\n- **LLR-262, LLR-306, LLR-310:** both adjudication routes now record that outcome. The loop does it in `adjudication_bookkeeping`; the coordinator's entry point records \"accepted\" only for a valid in-deadline verdict and \"failed\" for everything else, including an empty reservation. The binding has one writer (`write_binding`) and one recorder (`record_outcome`).\n- **LLR-307 and TC-326:** only an accepted, bound, valid verdict releases a Done-when hold. A failed or pending call releases nothing, and TC-326 gains six tests for those cases.\n- **LLR-278 and TC-278:** a held-rung re-attestation is now refused unless its verdict is accepted. A CLARITY line inside a verdict that is invalid as a whole no longer carries one, and there's a test for exactly that case.\n\nEach change narrows what counts as a verdict, so a pending or failed call can't release a hold or carry a re-attestation. The code in `170ee196` matches, and the cited tests exist.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `f85ac5fd` — the verdict file `012-ADJUDICATE-327adae.md`, with the trailer `WI: WI-841`.\n- `e9e5f846` — the re-attestation: `intake.py snapshot --reattests` naming all seven rows, which copied both registries and recorded act seq 52 in the act ledger.\n\nThe snapshot wasn't refused, so nothing else in either registry has drifted. The pre-commit checks passed on both commits.\n\n**For the coordinator:** `012-ADJUDICATE-327adae.md.requested`, the binding for this sitting, is still untracked and reads `outcome = pending`. Under the new rule the route records accepted or failed and commits it, so I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":337560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679},"output_tokens":734,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cffbbc6-0175-4e90-b9ab-7b165e0c0246","uuid":"62d8e54a-aee5-4136-9ad8-c21625237adf","timestamp":"2026-10-07T06:25:58.924Z","request_id":"req_011CfnQAA8eC8h6YwFd3ZKvz"}
